  "findings": [
    "A concrete native SendState records checked and attempted state. A shallow unchanged adapter alone could not support a growing observation projection; the local ready predicate also avoids treating rejected duplicate submissions as new attempts.",
    "Actual guarded Write helper tests cover zero-byte failure, partial acceptance, flush failure and a rejected second submission. Returned send/parser errors for writes remain OutcomeUnknown.",
    "Thirty regenerated stamp/driver/send-state/simulation obligations pass the named axiom audit. Six freshly extracted Rust mutants are rejected, including ignored repeated raw calls and stamp construction without authorization.",
    "AdmissionStamp avoids shadowing the older Lean Current predicate. A Boolean simp loop was fixed by case reduction and direct equality symmetry without weakening the theorem or raising kernel resource limits.",
    "The ordinary release gate uses the same pytest selection with explicit correct release BINARIES paths; the quick runner itself deliberately installs debug paths."
  ],
  "next-acceptance": "NR-2: instantiate native primitive/effect contracts and compose the staged provider with audit refusal, all complete request shapes, disclosure, completion/late-denial/guest-frame effects and connected session histories.",
  "remaining-obligations": [
    "Conditional callback contracts concern a projected provider-attempt trace. Native marks-to-Write correspondence, std/rustls/context conversion, transitive effects and other sinks are not proved merely from result/state equality.",
    "Non-returning, panic, drop/unwind, timeout and partial network delivery prefixes remain external obligations; a mark is not successful provider arrival.",
    "The same runtime target still needs complete request/history simulation, NR-3 sink/dependency closure, NR-4 actual/adaptive observations and NR-5 independent review.",
    "Real providers, deployed guest/host compartments and physical TPM provenance are not established by VM/synthetic acceptance."
  ],
